==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Ghost Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ghost Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ghost Baa Baa]]s spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.
*2 [[Bore]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Lord Enma]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Le'saint]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and/or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] for the Bores and a rusher like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] for Lord Enma. Because of Lord Enma's decently long TBA, Awakened Bahamut will be able to kill it in one go albeit it will be knocked back once. Once Lord Enma is taken care of, all that's left is Le'saint which is absolutely destroyed by [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]. Any anti-Angel units will speed up the process but are not necessary.

==Trivia==
*In Greek mythology, Cerberus is a three-headed dog that guards the gates to the underworld.
*The Japanese name refers to the Sanzu River, a river in Japanese Buddhist tradition and religious belief which the souls of the deceased must cross before they can reach the afterlife.

